  "title": "Pick one",
  "format": "build",
  "skills": [
    "logic.multiplexer"
  ],
  "brief": {
    "story": "The amplifier has two inputs (A: radio, B: phone) and a selector switch S. When S is off you hear A, when it’s on you hear B. That’s a 2-to-1 multiplexer, and four NAND gates make one. The last gate isn’t connected.",
    "goal": "Wire gates 2 and 3 into gate 4 so OUT = A when S is off, and B when S is on.",
    "datasheet": {
      "title": "Mux from 4 NANDs",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Gate 1",
          "NOT S → pin 3"
        ],
        [
          "Gate 2",
          "NAND(A, NOT S) → pin 6 (column 15)"
        ],
        [
          "Gate 3",
          "NAND(B, S) → pin 8 (column 16, bottom)"
        ],
        [
          "Gate 4",
          "pins 12, 13 (columns 12, 11, bottom) → OUT"
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "hints": [
    "Gates 2 and 3 each let one input through (inverted) when it’s selected. Gate 4 NANDs them back together: NAND of two NANDs is an OR of ANDs.",
    "Gate 4’s inputs are pin 12 (column 12, bottom half) and pin 13 (column 11, bottom half).",
    "Column 15 top (pin 6) → column 12 bottom (pin 12), and column 16 bottom (pin 8) → column 11 bottom (pin 13)."
  ],
