  "debrief": "A multiplexer picks one of several inputs with a select line: (A AND NOT S) OR (B AND S), here in four NANDs. Inside every CPU, multiplexers choose which register feeds the adder; on a board, they let one microcontroller pin read eight sensors in turn."
